{"step_index":181,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T12:32:51Z","content":"You got it! I just deployed a massive update to your app. Since it's already connected to your GitHub, if you refresh the page, you'll see all these new features live:\n\n### 1. 📊 Interactive Charts (Visual Setups)\nI've integrated the `plotly` library to generate interactive Candlestick charts right inside the app! \nNow, whenever a stock is flagged as a `BUY SIGNAL` or `WATCH`, a dropdown menu will appear below the table. When you click it, it will draw the exact chart showing:\n*   **The EMA 30 Lifeline** (Orange)\n*   **The Consolidation Box limits** (Blue and Purple dashed lines)\n*   Your exact **Entry, TP, and CL** plotted directly on the graph so you can visually confirm the setup without leaving the app!\n\n### 2. ⚡ Insanely Fast Data Caching\nTo stop the app from freezing up when you switch tabs or rerun the screener, I implemented a robust caching engine. It will now remember the stock data it downloaded for the next hour. This means running scans will feel almost instantaneous after the first time!\n\n### 3. ⭐ Jack's Technical Scoring System (/5)\nIn Chapter 18 (评分机制), Jack talks about scoring stocks to decide if they are worth your money. \nI have built an auto-scorer into the results table! It grades the stock out of 5 based on technicals (e.g., +2 for being above EMA 30, +1 for Volume Surge, +1 for tight Consolidation, +1 for Breakout). Now you can easily tell the difference between a mediocre setup and a perfect one!\n\n### 4. 📥 Download to CSV\nJack strongly advises keeping an Excel record of your trades (Chapter 21: *用 Microsoft Excel 建立一份“年度”交易记录*). \nI added a simple **\"Download CSV\"** button under the scanner results. You can now download the day's signals straight into Excel to keep a log!\n\n### 5. 🧹 Cleaned-up Interface\nI took all the tutorials, explanations, and strategy formulas, and packed them into a neat **\"📚 App Tutorials & Strategy Explanations\"** collapsible dropdown at the very top of the page. It’s completely out of your way until you need it!\n\nGive it a refresh at **http://localhost:8501** (or on your phone via the Streamlit Cloud link) and check out the new charts!"}
